.TH MODBUS-SCRAPER-CTL 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-scraper-ctl \- send commands to the modbus-scraper control server
(one-shot / batch)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-scraper-ctl
.RI [ options ] " [command ...]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends one command (or a batch from stdin) to modbus-scraper's JSON-lines
control server over TCP or a unix socket, prints the replies, exits. The
one-shot sibling of \fBmodbus-scraper-cli\fR(1): no session, no
completion — the scriptable surface (the exit codes, one reply per
command). With a control token configured the wire is HMAC-signed: the
client signs every command and verifies every reply (the full sha256 of
the frame, keyed by the token).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
control server target: unix socket path or TCP port on 127.0.0.1,
auto\-detected (default: /tmp/modbus\-scraper\-9350.socket; env CTL when
unset) — same flag as the scraper itself
.TP
.B command
control command, e.g. inspect, show status, set interval 5, poll now,
request reload, restart, shutdown
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
socket timeout in seconds (default 5.0)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
control auth token for TCP (env CONTROL_TOKEN); a file:<path> value
reads the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
audit trail: a file path or \- for stdout; default: the XDG state home
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size, 0 = off (default: 10.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the audit trail (default: off)


.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-scraper-cli (1),
.BR modbus-scraper (1)
